CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S-v2)

Preamble
CERN has developed this Licence to promote collaborating on the hardware
which we design and use. Although the words which follow are legal
language, our spirit is simple: we want everyone to be able to use the
designs which we share, but we also want you to share back any
improvements which you make.

1 Definitions
1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-S.
1.2 'Source' means information such as design materials, schematics,
instructions, CAD files and other documentation that is used to create
the Product.
1.3 'Product' means any physical object designed or manufactured using
the Source.
1.4 'You' means an individual or entity exercising rights under this
Licence.
1.5 'Licensee' means You, once You have accepted this Licence.
1.6 'Contributor' means a person or entity that releases changes to the
Source under this Licence.
1.7 'Make Available' means to provide or offer access to the Source or
Product to any third party.

2 Grant of Rights
2.1 Contributor grants You a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable copyright and patent licence to use,
copy, modify, communicate, and Make Available the Source, subject to the
conditions below.

3 Conditions and Reciprocal Obligations
3.1 If You Make Available modified Source, You must release all Your
modifications under this same CERN-OHL-S Licence.
3.2 If You Make Available Products (such as manufactured 3D prints or parts)
based on this Source or modified Source, You must Make Available the complete
corresponding Source to every recipient of the Product under this Licence.
3.3 You must maintain all copyright notices, license notices, and design
credits on all copies of Source and on physical Products where technically
feasible.

4 Disclaimer and Limitation of Liability
4.1 The Source is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express
or implied.
